error[E925]: `await` cannot be used in a default argument
 --> main/main.kg:4:21
  |
4 | async fn h(x: Int = await h2()) -> Int { x } //~ ERROR `await` cannot be used in a default argument
  |                     ^^^^^^^^^
  = help: the caller evaluates a default, and it need not be async even when the function is; take the future as the parameter and await it in the body

error[E712]: `?` requires a `Result` return type
 --> main/main.kg:7:13
  |
7 |     let a = f() //~ ERROR `?` requires a `Result` return type
  |             ^
  = help: this returns `Void`
note: the default of `x` uses `?`, so a call that omits it propagates the error to its caller
